OpenRadome
Copyright (C) 2026 Phillip and contributors

OpenRadome is a Rust reimplementation of readsb, the ADS-B and Mode S decoder maintained by
Matthias Wirth (wiedehopf): https://github.com/wiedehopf/readsb

OpenRadome is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU
General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License,
or (at your option) any later version. See COPYING for the full text.

It is not a fork and shares no history with readsb, but its decoding, tracking and output logic is
ported from readsb's source, and its behaviour and file formats follow readsb's. The copyright of
that work belongs to its authors, credited here as readsb credits them.


